# A pre-registration is hashed, and the hash is committed in the script that
# refuses to run on a changed file. core.autocrlf on a Windows checkout turned
# every LF into CRLF and the run refused a file nobody had edited (3a-3b).
# The hash now normalises line endings before hashing; this keeps the bytes
# the same on every platform as well.
BB3_PREREGISTRATION.md text eol=lf
*_PREREGISTRATION.md text eol=lf

# W0b: the pre-run data fixture is bytes captured once and pinned by sha256 in
# its MANIFEST.json; a Windows checkout must not rewrite the snapshot JSON's
# line endings, or the digest and the sealed snapshot no longer match.
tests/fixtures/pre_run_data/** -text

# W5: the injection set is hashed, and the hash was registered before the
# gateway's code. A Windows checkout gave it CRLF line endings and the harness
# refused it at collection (the closing run of 16 November). The harness now
# hashes the text with LF line endings; this keeps the checkout's bytes the
# same on every platform as well.
run/specs/W5_injection_set.json text eol=lf
tests/fixtures/W5_injection_set.json text eol=lf

# W11d: the specification's vectors are named by the SHA-256 of their bytes
# (docs/TALIMA_SPEC.md, section 14), and one of them is content whose line
# ends are part of what a commitment is over. No checkout may rewrite them:
# they are kept exactly as committed. (The test that reads the digests also
# reads a JSON vector's line ends back as LF, for a checkout made before this
# rule.)
tests/fixtures/tb_golden/** -text
tests/fixtures/w11d/** -text

# Amendment 11: the marks are published with their sha256 (docs/brand/README.md). No checkout may rewrite them:
# they are kept exactly as committed. (The test that reads the hashes reads each mark as git's index holds it, so
# a checkout's line ends do not change what it reads, and a mark committed with CRLF is named.)
docs/brand/*.svg -text
